The patch introduces an overlong reel and reuses the cover B-roll path for the final block, which can produce incorrect output and break the editing workflow. It also removes the tracked source URL needed to reproduce the official-page footage.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Keep the reel within the 50–55 second budget — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\episodes\2026-10-22-cumul-emploi-retraite\script.json:19-20
  The updated block durations sum to about 77.9 seconds and the narration contains 193 words, exceeding the documented 50–55 second and 140–150 word format. This will produce an overlong reel; shorten the narration and blocks before publishing (see `CLAUDE.md:174-184`).

- [P2] Give the final block a distinct B-roll file — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\episodes\2026-10-22-cumul-emploi-retraite\script.json:161-163
  Both the cover block and the final recommendation block use `B0.mp4`. On a clean checkout, preparation will reuse the cover footage, and `broll.py choisir` for the final block can overwrite the cover file; this also violates the repository rule against reusing a shooting (see `CLAUDE.md:250-253`).

- [P2] Preserve the official page URL in the script — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\episodes\2026-10-22-cumul-emploi-retraite\script.json:20-21
  Replacing the exact Service Public URL with a generic search description makes the B1 page shot unreproducible: `pages/` and B-roll files are ignored, so a clean checkout no longer has the source URL needed to regenerate it. Keep the URL in the `requete` field, as `scripts/page.py` does when creating official-page captures.
The patch introduces an overlong reel and reuses the cover B-roll path for the final block, which can produce incorrect output and break the editing workflow. It also removes the tracked source URL needed to reproduce the official-page footage.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Keep the reel within the 50–55 second budget — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\episodes\2026-10-22-cumul-emploi-retraite\script.json:19-20
  The updated block durations sum to about 77.9 seconds and the narration contains 193 words, exceeding the documented 50–55 second and 140–150 word format. This will produce an overlong reel; shorten the narration and blocks before publishing (see `CLAUDE.md:174-184`).

- [P2] Give the final block a distinct B-roll file — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\episodes\2026-10-22-cumul-emploi-retraite\script.json:161-163
  Both the cover block and the final recommendation block use `B0.mp4`. On a clean checkout, preparation will reuse the cover footage, and `broll.py choisir` for the final block can overwrite the cover file; this also violates the repository rule against reusing a shooting (see `CLAUDE.md:250-253`).

- [P2] Preserve the official page URL in the script — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\episodes\2026-10-22-cumul-emploi-retraite\script.json:20-21
  Replacing the exact Service Public URL with a generic search description makes the B1 page shot unreproducible: `pages/` and B-roll files are ignored, so a clean checkout no longer has the source URL needed to regenerate it. Keep the URL in the `requete` field, as `scripts/page.py` does when creating official-page captures.
